Photorealistic scene of a vast, intricate sandcastle city sprawling across a golden beach at golden hour, with multiple towers, walls, and archways casting long shadows. In the foreground, adult hands covered in wet sand are carefully shaping a detailed turret, while nearby a child's smaller hands pat down a wall section. Scattered around are simple wooden tools, buckets, and carved channels filled with seawater reflecting the warm sunset sky. The sandcastle complex shows various stages of completion—some sections pristine and architectural, others crumbling back into formless mounds. Ocean waves lap gently in the background, a reminder of impermanence. The lighting is warm and atmospheric, emphasizing texture in every grain of sand, water droplets on skin, and the satisfying density of well-packed wet sand. Focus on the tactile, meditative quality of hands-on creation.
